<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 18 June, from 618 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/618">618 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,408 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Li Yuan proclaims himself emperor, founding the Tang dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang">Li Yuan</a> took the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> as Emperor Gaozu. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a> presided over one of the most brilliant periods of Chinese culture.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">860 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,166 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Rus' fleet sails into the Bosphorus and raids Constantinople's suburbs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Rus' fleet of about 200 vessels sailed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosphorus">Bosphorus</a> and began pillaging the suburbs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. It was the only major Rus' expedition recorded in Byzantine and western European sources, and its outcome is unknown in detail.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosphorus">Bosphorus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1391">1391 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">635 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Timur defeats Tokhtamysh at the Kondurcha River</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a long march across the steppe, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> defeated his former protégé <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a>, khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>, near the Kondurcha River east of present-day Samara. Together with a second defeat on the Terek in 1395, it ruined the Horde.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-kondurcha-river">Battle of the Kondurcha River</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh-timur-war">Tokhtamysh–Timur war</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1429">1429 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">597 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles VII's army defeats the English at Patay</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The French vanguard, led by La Hire and Jean Poton de Xaintrailles, defeated an English army at Patay, the culmination of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> Campaign. The English lost 2,200 men, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-talbot-1st-earl-of-shrewsbury">John Talbot</a> was among the senior commanders captured.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vii-of-france">Charles VII of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-talbot-1st-earl-of-shrewsbury">John Talbot, 1st Earl of Shrewsbury</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1812">1812 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">United States declares war on Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Madison signed the declaration after Congress narrowly voted for war. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-1812">War of 1812</a> ended in stalemate in 1815, but gave Americans 'The Star-Spangled Banner'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wellington and Blücher defeat Napoleon at Waterloo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The arrival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher">Blücher</a>'s Prussians broke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s final assault on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wellington">Wellington</a>'s army near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>. Napoleon abdicated four days later and was exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-helena">St Helena</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">De Gaulle calls on the French to fight on</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking on the BBC from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a> rejected the coming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> and urged French forces to continue resistance. The appeal founded the Free French movement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1979">1979 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">47 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Carter and Brezhnev sign the SALT II treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The treaty capped each side's strategic nuclear launchers. The US Senate never ratified it after the Soviet invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, though both sides largely observed its limits.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 18 June <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-gonzalez-flores"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-gonzalez-flores.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel González Flores</span><span class="tp">1833–1893</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/miklos-horthy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/miklos-horthy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Miklós Horthy</span><span class="tp">1868–1957</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georgi-dimitrov"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georgi-dimitrov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georgi Dimitrov</span><span class="tp">1882–1949</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fernando-henrique-cardoso"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fernando-henrique-cardoso.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fernando Henrique Cardoso</span><span class="tp">b. 1931</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ronald-venetiaan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ronald-venetiaan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ronald Venetiaan</span><span class="tp">b. 1936</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 18 June <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rogier-van-der-weyden"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rogier-van-der-weyden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rogier van der Weyden</span><span class="tp">c. 1399–1464</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/piet-heyn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/piet-heyn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Piet Heyn</span><span class="tp">1577–1629</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jeanne-mance"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jeanne-mance.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jeanne Mance</span><span class="tp">1606–1673</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thomas-picton"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thomas-picton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thomas Picton</span><span class="tp">1758–1815</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/roald-amundsen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/roald-amundsen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Roald Amundsen</span><span class="tp">1872–1928</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
